-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",16,{
[481]="7003A690\n1\tCollect horse-feed from the container\tThere is a bag of horse-feed near the refugee waiting at the end of the line on the bridge trying to get into Gapholt. You should collect horse-feed from the bag.\n2\tMany horses are agitated by the wait on the bridge after the long journey from Woodhurst. The refugee at the end of the line suggested that you feed them to help calm them down.\t\n3\tComplete\tThe horses are now much less agitated thanks to your efforts.\n",
[482]="70044294\n1\tTalk to Merethien, Master Foodmonger, in the Dome of the Sun\tMerethien, the Master Foodmonger of the Council, is in the Dome of the Sun. Arodor told you that Merethien could use your assistance.\n2\tTalk to Mirudal, Warden of the Stores, in the Dome of the Sun\tMirudal, the Warden of the Stores, is in the Dome of the Sun. Arodor told you that Mirudal could use your assistance.\n3\tFind the entrance to the Upper Stores, in the north-east section of the Fifth Circle\tThe Upper Stores are located in the north-east section of the Fifth Circle of the city. Mirudal gave you an inventory with which you can take stock of the goods within the Upper Stores.\n4\tTalk to Túlharil outside the Upper Stores, in the north-east section of the Fifth Circle\tThe Upper Stores are located in the north-east section of the Fifth Circle of the city. Mirudal gave you an inventory with which you can take stock of the goods within the Upper Stores.\n5\tGo to the very back of the Upper Stores and use the Upper Stores Inventory\tInside the Upper Stores, you should compare the inventory with the actual goods being stored. Only by knowing the exact count of the foodstuffs available can Mirudal and Merethien properly ration them during a long siege.\n6\tFind the entrance to the Lower Stores, just north of the main gate to the city, in the First Circle\tThe Lower Stores are located just north of the main gate to the city, in the First Circle. Mirudal gave you an inventory with which you can take stock of the goods within the Lower Stores.\n7\tTalk to Dírion outside the Lower Stores, in the First Circle of the city\tThe Lower Stores are located just north of the main gate to the city, in the First Circle. Mirudal gave you an inventory with which you can take stock of the goods within the Lower Stores.\n8\tGo to the very back of the Lower Stores and use the Lower Stores Inventory\tInside the Lower Stores, you should compare the inventory with the actual goods being stored. Only by knowing the exact count of the foodstuffs available can Mirudal and Merethien properly ration them during a long siege.\n9\tTalk to Dírion outside the Lower Stores, in the First Circle of the city\tDírion is outside the Lower Stores, just north of the main gate to the city, in the First Circle. You have discovered that the inventory of the Lower Stores does not match their contents: some food is missing.\n10\tReturn the inventories to Mirudal in the Dome of the Sun, and tell him about the rats\tThe Dome of the Sun is in the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith. Dírion told you that he suspects rats have gotten into the Stores, and that explains the missing food. He asked you to tell Mirudal about it. The Warden of the Stores may want to lower his expectations for the food-rationing to come, as a result of the rats.\n11\tConfront Dírion outside the Lower Stores, in the First Circle\tThe Lower Stores are located just north of the main gate to the city, in the First Circle. Something about Dírion's story does not convince you, and you think you should confront the guard about it.\n",
[483]="70044297\n1\tTalk to Mirudal in the Dome of the Sun and tell him that Dírion will take care of the rats\tMirudal, the Warden of the Stores, is in the Dome of the Sun. You have agreed to help Dírion with his deception, so that his family can have the food he stole for them. He asked you to tell Mirudal that he will take care of the rats, and the Warden need not worry about them any longer.\n2\tTalk to Dírion outside the Lower Stores, in the First Circle\tDírion is outside the Lower Stores, located just north of the main gate to the city, in the First Circle. Mirudal, Warden of the Stores, has asked you to thank Dírion for his duty to the city.\n",
[484]="70044296\n1\tTalk to Thalhír in the Dome of the Sun\tThalhír, the Warden of Laws, is in the Dome of the Sun. You have decided to report of Dírion's transgression to Thalhír, the Warden of Laws.\n",
[485]="70057F69\n1\tExamine Boromir's horn\tBoromir's horn lies before Faramir in Merethrond. Faramir has asked you to inspect the horn of his fallen brother, Boromir.\n2\tTalk to Faramir\tFaramir can be found in Merethrond. You inspected Boromir's horn as Faramir asked. You should talk to Faramir.\n3\tBury the stone in the soil beside the sapling of the White Tree\tThe sapling of the White Tree can be found before the Tower of Ecthelion outside Merethrond. Faramir has asked you to bury a stone among the soil of the sapling of the White Tree.\n4\tTalk to Faramir\tFaramir can be found in Merethrond. You have done as Faramir asked. You should return to Faramir in Merethrond.\n",
[486]="70057F64\n1\tCollect a writing-quill\030Collect a phial of ink\030Collect sheets of parchment (total: 4)\tWriting-quills, phials of ink, and sheets of parchment might be found in either the Houses of Lore or the Blue Theatre. Frodo has asked you to gather a writing-quill, a phial of ink, and some sheets of parchment that he might begin to write on his adventures.\n2\tDeliver the quill, ink, and parchment to Frodo in Merethrond\tFrodo Baggins can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). You have collected the writing-quill, phial of ink, and parchment. You should deliver them to Frodo at the wedding banquet in Merethrond.\n3\tWait for Frodo to decide how to start his tale of adventure\tFrodo is deciding where to begin his tale of adventure.\n4\tTalk to Frodo\tFrodo Baggins can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). After delivering a quill, ink, and parchment to Frodo Baggins, he appears to have found himself unable to write. You should talk to Frodo.\n",
[487]="70057F6B\n1\tDrink with Gimli\tA pitcher of ale can be found at Gimli's table in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). Gimli has asked you to drink with him as he shares his plans for the coming days.\n2\tListen to Gimli\tGimli can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). You have shared a drink with Gimli and should now listen to him.\n3\tDrink with Gimli again\tA pitcher of ale can be found at Gimli's table in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). Gimli has again asked you to drink with him as he shares his plans for the coming days.\n4\tListen to Gimli\tGimli can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). You have shared another drink with Gimli and should again listen to him.\n5\tTalk to Gimli\tGimli can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). Gimli has finished telling of his plans for the comings days, but it seems he wishes to say something else to you.\n6\tTalk to Galadriel\tGaladriel can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). Gimli has asked you to speak to Galadriel on his behalf and see if she might wish to visit the Glittering Caves or return to Minas Tirith once the city gates are repaired.\n7\tTalk to Gimli\tGimli can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). Although seemingly flattered, Galadriel has politely declined Gimli's invitation. However, Galadriel did impart that she knows their paths shall cross once again.\n",
[488]="70057F6A\n1\tQuiet tables in Merethrond (total: 14)\tUnquieted tables can be found throughout Merethrond. King Aragorn II Elessar has asked you to quiet tables in Merethrond that he might offer a toast.\n2\tTalk to King Aragorn II Elessar\tKing Aragorn II Elessar can be found in Merethrond. You have quieted all of the tables in the main hall of Merethrond. You should return to King Aragorn II Elessar.\n",
[489]="70057F66\n1\tTalk to Gimli\tGimli can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). Legolas has asked you to invite Gimli to join him in a contest of fortitude at the wedding banquet. You should talk to Gimli.\n2\tTalk to Legolas\tLegolas can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). Gimli has politely declined Legolas's invitation. You should return to Legolas.\n3\tCollect bottles of wine in Merethrond (total: 10)\tBottles of wine can be found in the kitchens of Merethrond. Legolas has asked you to collect bottles of wine in Merethrond.\n4\tChallenge Gimli to 'battle' Legolas\tGimli can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). You have collected ten bottles of wine as Legolas asked. You should now challenge Gimli to 'battle' Legolas in a contest of fortitude.\n5\tTalk to Gimli\tGimli can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). Your challenge seems to have gotten Gimli's attention. You should talk to Gimli.\n6\tTalk to Legolas\tLegolas can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). Gimli has enthusiastically accepted Legolas's challenge. You should talk to Legolas.\n",
[490]="70057F63\n1\tSearch for Merry's pipe-weed in the Southern Great Guest-house\030Search for Merry's pipe-weed in the High Stables\030Search for Merry's pipe-weed on the prow of Minas Tirith\tMerry's pipe-weed might be found near the baths in the Southern Great Guest-house, among the High Stables, or near the end of the prow of Minas Tirith. Merry has asked you to find his supply of Longbottom Leaf in Minas Tirith.\n2\tReturn to Merethrond\tMerethrond can be found near the Tower of Ecthelion in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). You did not find Merry's pipe-weed in any of the locations he mentioned. You should return to Merethrond and inform him.\n3\tTalk to Toldir\tToldir can be found in Merethrond. Upon entering Merethrond, Toldir tried to get your attention. You should talk to Toldir.\n4\tCollect Merry's pipe-weed in Merethrond\tMerry's pipe-weed can be found at the base of the stairs to the kitchens in Merethrond. Toldir informed you that he left Merry's pipe-weed in the kitchens of Merethrond. You should collect it.\n5\tDeliver the pipe-weed to Meriadoc Brandybuck\tMerry can be found in Merethrond. You have collected Merry's pipe-weed and should now return it to him.\n",
[491]="70057F65\n1\tCollect 'On the Line of Kings' in the High Guest-house\030Collect the 'Chronicle of Arnor' in the High Guest-house\t'On the Line of Kings' and the 'Chronicle of Arnor' can be found in Mithrandir's guest-chamber in the High Guest-house. Mithrandir has asked you to collect two tomes from his guest-chamber in the High Guest-house and return them to him in Merethrond.\n2\tDeliver the tomes of lore to Mithrandir in Merethrond\tMithrandir can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). You have found the tomes that Mithrandir requested and should now deliver them to him at the wedding banquet.\n3\tTalk to Mithrandir\tMithrandir can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). Mithrandir has not revealed why he needed the tomes from his guest-chamber. You should wait and see if he will soon reveal their purpose.\n4\tTalk to Mithrandir\tMithrandir can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). Mithrandir seems prepared to discuss the purpose of the tomes he requested from his guest-chamber. You should talk to Mithrandir.\n",
[492]="70057F68\n1\tVarious platters of food can be found in the kitchens of Merethrond. Pippin has asked you to gather food from the kitchens of Merethrond that it might be give to the children and refugees seeking shelter in the Old Guest-house.\t\n2\tTravel to the Old Guest-house\tThe Old Guest-house can be found in the First Circle to the south of the gates of Minas Tirith (Midsummer). Pippin has asked you to deliver the food you collected to the inhabitants of the Old Guest-house.\n3\tDeliver the platters of food to the children at the Old Guest-house\tThe children can be found just outside the Old Guest-house in the First Circle of Minas Tirith (Midsummer). You have arrived at the Old Guest-house with the platters of food you gathered in Merethrond. You should offer it to the children that they might share it with the other inhabitants of the Old Guest-house.\n4\tTalk to Pippin\tPippin can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). You successfully delivered the platters of food to the inhabitants of the Old Guest-house. You should return to Pippin.\n5\tDeliver the sealed missive to Beregond\tBeregond can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). Pippin has asked you to give a sealed missive to Beregond.\n6\tTalk to Pippin\tPippin can be found in Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). Beregond has learned the truth of his invitation to the wedding of King Aragorn II Elessar and Arwen Undómiel. You should talk to Pippin.\n",
[493]="70057F62\n1\tMeet Samwise Gamgee in a small alcove in Merethrond\tSamwise Gamgee can be found in a small alcove of Merethrond, across from the High King and High Queen's table and down the stairs. Samwise Gamgee has asked you to accompany him to a small alcove in Merethrond where he wishes to speak further to you.\n2\tTalk to Samwise Gamgee\tSamwise Gamgee can be found in a small alcove of Merethrond, across from the High King and High Queen's table and down the stairs. You have found Samwise Gamgee in a quiet alcove beneath the main hall of Merethrond. You should talk to Samwise Gamgee.\n3\tSamwise's worrisome thoughts can be found throughout Merethrond. Samwise Gamgee has begun to worry about the friends and family he left behind in the Shire. You should help him dispel these worrisome thoughts.\t\n4\tTalk to Samwise Gamgee\tSamwise Gamgee can be found in a small alcove of Merethrond, across from the High King and High Queen's table and down the stairs. You have helped Samwise dispel his worrisome thoughts of the Shire. You should talk to Samwise Gamgee.\n",
[494]="70057F67\n1\tTalk to one of the attendees at the banquet in Merethrond\tAttendees of the banquet can be found throughout Merethrond in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). NOTE: You must complete a quest for one of the guests at the banquet to advance this quest.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have attended the banquet in Merethrond and mingled with one of the many attendees before the night was ended.\n",
[495]="70068327\n1\tIthurga suspects this is a replica and wants you to confirm all the rumours about this hammer from the town's residents.\t\n2\tConfirm witness accounts 7/8\tAll the witnesses had varying tales, but a professor has told us Shereb knows of this hammer. You can find Shereb in the most isolated part of Halrax.\n3\tTalk to Ithurga\tYou've gathered all the information you can from the townsfolk of Halrax. You now have a lead. You should talk to Ithurga. Ithurga can be found in Halrax.\n",
[496]="700450F9\n1\tMeet Gondrad at Bâr Nadhron\tMeet Gondrad before Jarl Akhiz's camp at Bâr Nadhron.\n2\tExplore the various entrances of Jarl Akhiz's camp in Bâr Nadhron.\t\n3\tReturn to Gondrad\tReturn to Gondrad just outside the camp at Bâr Nadhron.\n",
[497]="70046BFE\n1\tPatrol the hill-top to the north of Bâr Aroth\030Patrol the foot-hills of the Ephel Dúath to east of Bâr Aroth\030Patrol the shores of the Anduin to the north of Osgiliath\tBâr Aroth can be found on a hillside to the north of the Cross-roads in North Ithilien. Thurindol has asked you to assess the Enemy's presence in North Ithilien before you continue your journey to the refuge.\n2\tTalk to Thurindol at Aelin Veren\tThurindol can be found at Aelin Veren. You have scouted the lands surrounding Bâr Aroth and should bring news to Thurindol at Aelin Veren.\n",
[498]="70061775\n1\tHelp Athal with 'The Bounty-hunter of Lhúngobel'\030Help Erfith with 'A Deal Gone Wrong'\tAthal and Erfith can be found on a hill just off the road near the border of Ered Luin in Yondershire. Avorthal has asked you to aid Athal and the Dourhand, Erfith, in routing the goblins that have crossed into the Yondershire.\n2\tTalk to Avorthal\tAvorthal can be found on a hill just off the road near the border of Ered Luin in Yondershire. You have aided Avorthal and Athal in routing the goblins that crossed the River Lune, freed Erfith's peace-seeking companions, and learned of the Dourhands' plot to rally their wicked allies to the ancient keep of Sarnúr. You should talk to Avorthal.\n",
[499]="700000AE\n1\tTalk to Isferon\tIsferon is at the refuge of Duillond in Ered Luin. You have been told that Isferon has a puzzle that he cannot solve. As Isferon is a most learned Lore-master, this puzzle must be difficult indeed.\n2\tSolve Berenin's first riddle and collect a key from the correct location\tIsferon gave you the first of Berenin's riddles. Isferon hopes that you can discover the solution of Berenin's riddle and collect the first of three keys from the location that is described.\n3\tBring Berenin's first key to Isferon\tIsferon is at the refuge of Duillond in Ered Luin. Now that you have solved the first of three riddles given him by his friend Berenin, you should return the key you found to Isferon at Duillond.\n4\tSolve Berenin's second riddle and collect a key from the correct location\tIsferon gave you the second of Berenin's riddles. Isferon hopes that you can discover the solution of Berenin's riddle and collect the second of three keys from the location that is described.\n5\tBring Berenin's second key to Isferon\tIsferon is at the refuge of Duillond in Ered Luin. Now that you have solved the second of three riddles given him by his friend Berenin, you should return the key you found to Isferon at Duillond.\n6\tSolve Berenin's third riddle and collect a key from the correct location\tIsferon gave you the third of Berenin's riddles. Isferon hopes that you can discover the solution of Berenin's riddle and collect the last of the three keys from the location that is described.\n7\tBring Berenin's third key to Isferon\tIsferon is at the refuge of Duillond in Ered Luin. Now that you have solved the last of three riddles given him by his friend Berenin, you should return the key you found to Isferon at Duillond.\n8\tTalk to Isferon and travel with him to the cave\tIsferon is at the refuge of Duillond in Ered Luin. You have become a part of Isferon's quest to discover his friend Berenin's legacy by solving the riddles he left, and now Isferon waits to travel with you to the cave where he stored Berenin's locked boxes.\n9\tTalk to Isferon\tIsferon is at Duillond, the refuge in Ered Luin. You discovered Berenin's legacy -- a desire that he not be forgotten by his friend and to engage in one last game of riddles -- and helped Isferon not lose sight of his friend's memory. Isferon is waiting to speak with you again.\n",
[500]="7002C922\n1\tFind the site of Wynmar's grave to pay your respects\tWynmar's resting place lies a short distance south of the hunters' camp-site. You should find Wynmar's gravesite to pay your last respects to a bold and kind man.\n2\tAsk Noriel why she lingers\tNoriel is at Wynmar's grave. You should find out why Noriel lingers here.\n3\tPay your respects to Wynmar with a moment of silence\tWynmar's grave is upon the hilltop in the south of Thinglad. You should pay your respects at Wynmar's grave.\n4\tTalk to Noriel\tNoriel lingers at Wynmar's grave. You should speak with Noriel, now that you have paid your respects.\n",
[501]="700351D7\n1\tSearch for Duskleaf near the Enting Hollow\tDuskleaf can be found somewhere near the Enting Hollow in north-eastern Balewood. Nindorn has sent you in search of his lost friend, Duskleaf, and hopes to have him join in his journey to Stonecliff.\n2\tTalk to Duskleaf\tDuskleaf can be found at the Enting Hollow. Duskleaf has appeared from the shadows, and you should now speak with him and try to convince him to rejoin the other Ents.\n3\tTalk to Nindorn\tNindorn can be found in northern Balewood. You have defeated the maddened Duskleaf. You should bring these ill tidings to Nindorn.\n",
[502]="7003FF48\n1\tSearch for Dírion's dog near the Hill of Erech\tDírion's dog can be found somewhere east of Alagrant on the fields of Blackroot Vale. Sarnir has informed you that Dírion's hunting dog has gone missing, and has asked you to aid in its safe return.\n2\tTalk to Dírion\tDírion can be found in Alagrant in western Blackroot Vale. You have rescued Dírion's dog from the Dead near the Hill of Erech and should now deliver the good news to him.\n3\tTalk to Sarnir\tSarnir can be found in Alagrant in western Blackroot Vale. You have delivered Dírion's dog back into his care, and should now speak to Sarnir.\n",
[503]="70019D26\n1\tTalk to Hadhelen in Egladil\030Talk to Aesbrennil in Egladil\030Talk to Farasdúr in Egladil\030Talk to Glasnír in Egladil\tThere are Elves throughout Egladil. You should speak with the Elves in Egladil and learn to whom the finely-wrought necklace belongs.\n2\tTalk to Maliriel at Imlad Lalaith\tMaliriel is in Imlad Lalaith in Egladil. You should bring the necklace to Maliriel to see if she knows to whom it belongs.\n",
[504]="70048C77\n1\tExamine the first Drúadan statue\tKâwon-weni-Khûrs and his statues can be found in Bhol Rûdh. You should examine the Drúadan statues and listen to Kâwon-weni-Khûrs.\n2\tExamine the second Drúadan statue\tKâwon-weni-Khûrs and his statues can be found in Bhol Rûdh. You should examine the Drúadan statues and listen to Kâwon-weni-Khûrs.\n3\tExamine the third Drúadan statue\tKâwon-weni-Khûrs and his statues can be found in Bhol Rûdh. You should examine the Drúadan statues and listen to Kâwon-weni-Khûrs.\n4\tExamine the fourth Drúadan statue\tKâwon-weni-Khûrs and his statues can be found in Bhol Rûdh. You should examine the Drúadan statues and listen to Kâwon-weni-Khûrs.\n5\tTalk to Kâwon-weni-Khûrs\tKâwon-weni-Khûrs can be found in Bhol Rûdh. You should talk to Kâwon-weni-Khûrs.\n",
[505]="7002EDDC\n1\tHunt aurochs-bulls in the Entwash Vale\t\n2\tDefeat aurochs-bulls in the Entwash Vale (total: 4)\tAurochs-bulls can be found throughout the Entwash Vale, but especially in the herds to the south and the east of Eaworth. You believe you can collect a decent bounty for the hunting of aurochs-bulls.\n",
[506]="70062E7D\n1\tDefeat creatures in Ruddymore that pose a danger to folk nearby (total: 10)\tThe creatures that live in Ruddymore act with a madness they never have before, and must be dealt with before they do harm to the folk who live nearby.\n2\tTalk to Thornegil at Sarn Ford\tThornegil is at Sarn Ford.\n",
[507]="7006AA10\n1\tDefeat Fleet-fast ruffians (total: 6)\tA group of ruffians is causing trouble in the Fleet-fast near the Soldiers' Mess-hall. You should go there and teach them a lesson.\n2\tFind Râkariz and the deck-steward\tAt the nearby docks in the Fleet-fast, there is a dispute going on at one of the ships. A fruitmonger and a deck-steward are arguing about fruit shipment. You should find where they are.\n3\tInspect the shipment of fruit\tYou have found Râkariz and the deck-steward arguing about the shipment of fruit. You should inspect the fruit to see its condition.\n4\tTalk to Râkariz\tYou have inspected the fruit in question, and it is indeed rotten. You noticed a stamp that indicated the fruit came from Khûtra. You should confront the fruitmonger Râkariz.\n5\tTalk to Belondor in Dâr Laja\tYou have inspected the fruit and confronted Râkariz with the knowledge that provisions from Khûtra have somehow been corrupted after the fall of Mâkhda Khorbo. You should return to Belondor and tell him what you learned.\n",
[508]="7006AA11\n1\tFind the location Belondor described\tBelondor has asked you to enter Ilmabiri, beneath the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl, and locate his secret cache of savings.\n2\tCollect Belondor's cache\tYou have found the location Belondor described as the location of his hidden cache. You should retrieve the treasure.\n3\tBring the cache to Belondor in Dâr Laja\tYou have collected Belondor's secret cache from its hiding place in Ilmabiri. You should bring it to Belondor in Dâr Laja.\n",
[509]="7006AA12\n1\tTalk to Mêshka at the Fleet-watch Tavern\tMêshka has requested that you meet her at the Fleet-watch Tavern, located at the southern end of the Fleet-fast, across from the Old Bastion Inn.\n2\tScout near the Sailors' Mess-hall\030Scout the gate near the Parade Ground\030Scout between the Gate of Sorrows and the Stûna\030Scout near the Fleet-gate\030Scout near the Lord's Gate\tMêshka is commissioning a memorial for the crew of the Rebuke and has asked for your assistance in choosing a location.\n3\tTalk to Mêshka at the Fleet-watch Tavern\tYou have scouted several possible locations for Mêshka. You should return to her at the Fleet-watch Tavern at the southern end of the Fleet-fast to tell her your findings.\n",
[510]="7006AA13\n1\tConfront the person spying on you\tMêshka has spotted that the two of you are being watched. She suggests you confront the man at the Fleet-watch Tavern at the south end of the Fleet-fast.\n2\tTalk to Belondor in Dâr Laja\tTabrím, a member of the Order of the Eagle has asked you to bring an offer to Belondor.\n",
[511]="7006AA1D\n1\tCollect dues from the fruit peddler\030Collect dues from the cloth dealer\030Collect dues from the fishmonger\030Collect dues from the Old Bastion Innkeeper\030Collect dues from the Fleet-watch Tavern\tTalk to the traders in the Fleet-fast and collect their dues.\n2\tTalk to Belondor in Dâr Laja\tYou have collected the dues from the traders in the Fleet-fast. You should return to Belondor in Dâr Laja.\n",
[512]="7006AA32\n1\tTalk to Mêshka at the Fleet-watch Tavern\tMeet with Mêshka at the Fleet-watch Tavern.\n2\tTalk to Ansham, Talkênza's wife\030Talk to Bekhír, Khalmôz's son\030Talk to Okhâb, Hâkraph's brother\030Talk to Pârnakh, Mairan's mother\030Talk to Imâra, Sallax's wife\tMêshka has asked you to visit each of the surviving family members of the crew of the Rebuke and invite them to the memorial she arranged.\n3\tTalk to Mêshka at the Fleet-watch Tavern\tYou have invited the families of the slain crew members of the Rebuke. You should return to Mêshka at the Fleet-watch Tavern.\n4\tTalk to Mêshka\tEverything for the memorial has been prepared. You should talk to Mêshka when you are ready to attend.\n5\tTalk to Belondor in Dâr Laja\tThe memorial is now complete. It looks like Belondor wants to talk to you.\n",
})
